---
const preguntas = [
  ["Which agents can use it?", "Any agent that supports the Agent Skills standard and can run shell commands: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, GitHub Copilot in VS Code and many more. A chat without a terminal can draft docs but can't keep them verified, because it has no access to your repository."],
  ["Does my code leave my machine?", "No. DocKeeper makes no network calls. The seal file contains file paths, line numbers and hashes, never code."],
  ["Do I need an AI model to run the check?", "No. Your agent uses the skill to write documentation; the check itself is plain Python and runs anywhere, including CI."],
  ["What happens when I rename a function?", "Anchors to it report <code>CHANGED</code> (symbol not found). Update the anchor in the document and run <code>dockeeper scan</code>. Try it in the demo above."],
  ["Can it review every commit by itself?", "Yes. Ask your agent to “review the docs on every commit” and it installs a git <code>post-commit</code> hook that runs <code>dockeeper review</code>. It never blocks a commit; whoever commits sees which claims changed and what new code has no docs yet."],
  ["Does it work with monorepos?", "Yes. <code>audit</code> lists every package it finds by its manifest (npm, pnpm, Go, Cargo, Python, Maven, Gradle and more), and the agent documents them one at a time with <code>--solo</code>."],
  ["What should I commit?", "Your documents, <code>.dockeeper.json</code> if you use one, and <code>.dockeeper.sello.json</code>, the seal that CI checks against."],
  ["Is the CLI in English?", "Yes, by default, and in Spanish when your environment is (<code>LANG=es_…</code>). Verdict codes and the keys of the <code>--json</code> output are the same in both languages, so agents and scripts are not affected."],
];
---
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="label">FAQ</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Questions, answered.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      {preguntas.map(([pregunta, respuesta], i) => (
        <div data-reveal style={`--d:${(i % 2) * 80}ms`}><h3>{pregunta}</h3><p set:html={respuesta} /></div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
